diff --git a/CONTRIBUTING.md b/CONTRIBUTING.md
index 1ef249472cdca4f799a0e5efbed8dbe05927e356..398828bb6d6468d7c04679e4aa722adcdae3827f 100644
--- a/CONTRIBUTING.md
+++ b/CONTRIBUTING.md
@@ -29,7 +29,9 @@
 
 Argtable is bundled in `third_party/argtable3` as the upstream [v3.3.1](https://github.com/argtable/argtable3/tree/v3.3.1) amalgamation (commit `b50c6c81f25eef8af51141678b333c55b661414d`), with its license notices preserved. It is compiled statically; no external Argtable installation or download is required on any platform.
 
-On Unix-like systems, the unmodified [ncurses 6.6 sources](https://github.com/ThomasDickey/ncurses-snapshots/tree/v6_6_20251230) (commit `0096bd402c4a9c8f39bd7ed266e1b8920327e4d8`) are included directly in `third_party/ncurses`, with their license in `COPYING`. Meson builds only the static wide-character library (`ncursesw`), including its terminfo code, alongside astroterm. No system curses headers, curses libraries, source archives, or build-time downloads are used. Standard system terminfo data is still used at runtime; `TERMINFO` and `TERMINFO_DIRS` can specify alternate database locations. Windows continues to use PDCurses.
+On Unix-like systems, the unmodified [ncurses 6.6 sources](https://github.com/ThomasDickey/ncurses-snapshots/tree/v6_6_20251230) (commit `0096bd402c4a9c8f39bd7ed266e1b8920327e4d8`) are included directly in `third_party/ncurses`, with their license in `COPYING`. Meson builds only the static wide-character library (`ncursesw`), including its terminfo code, alongside astroterm. No system curses headers, curses libraries, source archives, or build-time downloads are used. Windows continues to use PDCurses.
+
+Terminal descriptions for `xterm`, `xterm-256color`, `screen`, `screen-256color`, `tmux`, `tmux-256color`, `linux`, `vt100`, `vt220`, `rxvt`, `rxvt-256color`, `kitty`, `alacritty`, `foot`, `foot-direct`, `wezterm`, `st`, and `st-256color` are embedded as fallbacks. They work even without a system terminfo database. Other terminal types require system terminfo data; `TERMINFO` and `TERMINFO_DIRS` can specify alternate database locations. The pre-generated `third_party/ncurses/fallback.c` was produced from the bundled `misc/terminfo.src` using ncurses 6.6's `ncurses/tinfo/MKfallback.sh`, `tic`, and `infocmp`; these tools are not required when building astroterm.
 
 > [!TIP]
 > See [`ci.yml`](./.github/workflows/ci.yml) for how `astroterm` is built and tested on Ubuntu via GitHub Actions.
